  "title": "Malala Yousafzai",
  "summary": "Malala Yousafzai is a Pakistani activist for female education who began speaking out against Taliban school closures in the Swat Valley as a schoolgirl. After surviving a 2012 assassination attempt by a Taliban gunman on her school bus, she became an international symbol of the right to education and was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 2014 at age seventeen, becoming the youngest Nobel laureate in history.",
